 "notes": "Votes of 5 default-parameter indicators (close>EMA50, MACD hist>0, RSI14>50, Supertrend(10,3) up, Aroon(14) osc>0) and a 7-vote version (+PSAR direction, close above Ichimoku cloud); K-of-N written as an 'any' of all K-subsets. NIFTY monthly futures, 1 lot, swing max_days 30, exit 1 day before expiry, 3xATR(1d) trailing underlying stop, no parameter tuning. DAILY PRE-CHECK 2012-2020 (pandas, index points, 3 pts/round trip + 3 pts per monthly roll, next-open fills; benchmark always-long with the same 3ATR trail = +9,040 pts, t 2.07, maxDD -3,402; buy&hold +9,327): long/short votes are weak (LS5 K3 +3,876 pts t 0.88; K4 +1,020; K5 +1,235; LS7 K4 +4,069 t 0.93; LS7 K5 +3,191) - the short side gives back what the long side earns. Long-only 'vote >= K, exit when it falls below K': K3 +6,130 t 2.19 maxDD -1,711; K4 +4,107 t 1.69; K5 +1,208 t 0.59; L7 K4 +5,915 t 2.12; hysteresis versions similar (+4,117 / +4,551). So the vote only halves drawdown versus always-long; it doesn't add return. Forward-return table by net score (bull minus bear count, 2012-2020): fully bearish (-5) days have ~0 next-day and +7 pts 10-day forward vs +33 for fully bullish and +52-84 for mixed scores, i.e. trend votes have no monotone predictive power on NIFTY daily (mixed states mean-revert upward). A rule picked from that table AFTER seeing it (long unless all 5 / all 7 bearish) did best in 2012-2020 (+8,590 t 2.61 / +9,801 t 2.75) - snooped. ENGINE 2021-2024 (Rs, lot sizes vary): benchmark always-long 3ATR +Rs249k t 0.93 PF 1.37 (80 trades). Every daily vote filter LOST to that benchmark: L5 K3 +98k t 0.56 (64 tr), L5 K4 +94k t 0.59, L7 K4 +93k t 0.53, long-unless-all-5-bearish +77k t 0.35, long-unless-all-7-bearish +161k t 0.65, LS5 K3 -110k t -0.42 (117 tr). The pandas sim on 2021-2024 agrees in points (bench +8,368 pts, L5 K3 +4,695, L5 K4 +3,912). 60m vote held multi-day (long-only K3 of 5, exit when 3 of 5 bearish on 60m): 194 trades, +Rs265k, PF 1.39, t 1.50, maxDD -169k (-28%), but net without best 5% = -Rs126k, 2024 lost (-29k), missing_data 27. 60m K4 + daily K3 filter: +111k t 0.91 (101 tr). 15m intraday long/short vote K4 aligned with daily K3, 2xATR(15m) trailing intraday stop, square-off 15:15: 1,153 trades, -Rs299k, PF 0.83, t -2.30, losing every year. Conclusion: on NIFTY, ensemble trend votes are a drawdown-reducing beta filter, not an edge; long-only versions depend on NIFTY drifting up and the short side has no edge in either period. NO candidates submitted. Near-miss EV7 listed under near_misses for information only; not recommended for a test look.",
 "platform_issues": [
  "K-of-N votes must be written as an 'any' of all C(N,K) 'all' groups (10 groups for 3-of-5, 35 for 4-of-7). An 'at_least: K' group (or a score operand summing boolean conditions) would make votes compact and likely faster: 60m/15m vote specs took ~2-4 min each over 2021-2024, daily ones ~70 s.",
  "exits.exit_signal is direction-agnostic, so a long/short vote can't exit with hysteresis (exit longs when bull votes < 3 while entering at >= 4); only exit_on_opposite_signal is available.",
  "60m swing specs report missing_data 12-27 on the snapshot (futures 1m gaps 2021-2024); 15m intraday 20 missing + 51 skipped."
 ],
